        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "No. 42 Dun Esker, Ballinasloe is a well-maintained four-bedroom, three-bathroom semi-detached home extending to approximately 123 sq. m (1,400 sq. ft). The property is presented in excellent condition and is ready for immediate occupation. It has an impressive B3 energy rating. This efficiency should save the new owner on heating and energy costs for years to come  and  may also makes the property eligible for an improved green mortgage rates.\r\n\r\nKey Features\r\n\r\nFour-bedroom, three-bathroom semi-detached homeGenerous\r\nSize - Extending to approximately 123 sq. m (1,400 sq. ft)\r\nB3 BER rating\r\nMains natural gas heating\r\nPVC double glazed windows throughout\r\nMaster bedroom with ensuite\r\nBuilt-in wardrobes in all-bedrooms\r\nLocated to the rear of the development in a low-traffic setting\r\nTarmac driveway with off-street parking for two cars\r\nSun-filled private rear garden \r\nA small, established development of about 40 houses with an on-site crèche.\r\nSuitable for both owner-occupiers and investors\r\n\r\nLocation.\r\n\r\nDun Esker is a small, established residential development in Ballinasloe, comprising approximately 40 homes and built around 2000. The estate is well maintained and has a settled residential feel. It received recognition in the Ballinasloe Tidy Towns awards in 2025. The development includes an onsite creche, which is convenient for families. The property is within walking distance of Ballinasloe town centre, Tesco and Portiuncula Hospital.\r\nNo. 42 is positioned towards the back of the estate, providing a quieter setting with less passing traffic.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\n\r\nThe front of the property has a tarmac driveway with parking for two cars and a lawn area. There is side access leading to the rear garden. The rear garden is private and benefits from all day sun, perfect for family living and entertaining.\r\n\r\nInside\r\n\r\nThe layout is practical and well balanced. \r\nThe entrance hallway leads to a sitting room at the front of the house with a gas fire. \r\nTo the rear, there is a kitchen and dining area with sliding doors opening onto the garden. A separate utility room with a back door and a guest WC complete the ground floor.\r\nUpstairs, there are four large bedrooms, all with built-in wardrobes. The main bedroom includes an ensuite. \r\nA family bathroom and hot press complete the first floor.\r\n\r\nNext Steps\r\n\r\nFor further information or to arrange a viewing, contact Kevin O Flynn Estate Agents and Auctioneers, Ballinasloe."
      },
